0017-glm-overlap-priority: TensorFold 0.6.2 port series (apply after the lower numbers, patch -p0 in the directory
that holds the installed tensorfold package).
Origin: MiaAI-Lab's patch (GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 recipe, Apache-2.0), first written for TensorFold 0.6.0.
Port: applied by a 3-way merge without conflict; the change is the 0.6.0 patch's, at 0.6.2's lines.
Files: families/glm5_next/cuda/hcsplit.py.

diff --git tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/hcsplit.py tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/hcsplit.py
index 0002a96..a294319 100644
--- tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/hcsplit.py
+++ tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/hcsplit.py
@@ -107,7 +107,9 @@ class HcSplit:
         self.got: list[torch.Tensor] = []
         self.stream = None
         if settings.overlap:
-            self.stream = torch.cuda.Stream(priority=-1)
+            # TF_GLM_OVERLAP_PRIORITY: the side stream's priority (-1 high, 0 normal); a high-priority stream in the
+            # process may cost decode rounds (graphs on the default stream) a little: measured per boot
+            self.stream = torch.cuda.Stream(priority=-1 if os.environ.get("TF_GLM_OVERLAP_PRIORITY", "-1").strip() != "0" else 0)
             n = settings.piece_count()
             self.ev_fill = [torch.cuda.Event() for _ in range(n)]
             self.ev_part = [torch.cuda.Event() for _ in range(n)]
